    <briefdescription>
<para>Gradient function for tensor-scalar division. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradDivideScalar" kindref="compound">GradDivideScalar</ref> class represents division operations involving a tensor and a scalar value in the computational graph, computing gradients for operations of the form <formula id="29">$C = A / s$</formula> or <formula id="30">$C = s / A$</formula> where <formula id="12">$A$</formula> is a tensor and <formula id="13">$s$</formula> is a scalar value. The numerator flag determines which form was used during the forward pass.</para>
<para>For the operation <formula id="29">$C = A / s$</formula> (numerator = true), the gradient computation follows from:   <formula id="31">\[    \frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = \frac{1}{s}
\]</formula> and during backpropagation:    <formula id="32">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \cdot
\frac{1}{s}
\]</formula></para>
<para>For the operation <formula id="30">$C = s / A$</formula> (numerator = false), the gradient computation follows from:   <formula id="33">\[    \frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = -\frac{s}{A^2}
\]</formula> and during backpropagation:    <formula id="34">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \odot
\left(-\frac{s}{A^2}\right)
\]</formula></para>
<para>This <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> saves the scalar value, a shared pointer to the tensor from the forward pass, and a flag indicating whether the tensor was the numerator or denominator, as all are required to compute the gradient during the backward pass.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> for the base class from which this class derives. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradDivide" kindref="compound">GradDivide</ref> for the gradient function for elementwise tensor division. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
